      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nREA Donohoe Spring is delighted to present to the market this Traditional Stone 4 Bed, 2 Storey Farmhouse with Range of Quality Outbuildings on C. 2.28 Acre Roadside Parcel. Scenic Peaceful Setting, Convenient to Cavan (N3), Ballyhaise Butlersbridge (N54). Requires Modernisation Qualifies for Vacant Property Grant. Would make a practical smallholding for livestock, horses or horticulture. For Sale By Private Treaty. \n\n \n\nRequiring renovation and qualifying for the vacant property grant amongst other, this traditional stone farm house is positioned centrally on the large 2.28 acre site was originally constructed over 150 years ago.\n\n \n\nThe living accommodation extends to C. 105 sqm/1,130 sqft comprises;\n\nGROUND FLOOR: Porch area (1.6 x 0.9), Entrance hall (3.9 x 1.0), Living room (4.6 x 3.4) with OFP, Kitchen (3.9 x 3.8) with oil fired range, Scullery/Utility (2.0 x 1.9), Bedroom 1 (3.9 x 2.5) with built in closet En-suite (2.1x 2.0). There is also an externally accessed cold store room (1.7 x 1.2).\n\nFIRST FLOOR: Landing (3.9 x 1.4), Bedroom 2 (4.9 x 3.8), Bedroom 3 (3.5 x 3.0), Bedroom 4 (3.8 x 3.0) Bathroom (2.7 x 1.8).\n\nThe property can be extended to the rear a further 41 sqm on the ground floor up to 20 sqm on the first floor, exempt from planning permission.\n\n \n\nBuilt of traditional stone construction, this solid residence also features a slate roof uPVC double glazed windows door. Requiring modernisation throughout, the property affords the opportunity for the new owners to really make it their own should qualify for a range of grants including the vacant property grant SEAI energy efficiency grants.\n\n \n\nServiced by; On-site septic tank, Group water connection Oil fired central heating. Located in a fibre broadband connected area. BER: G.\n\n \n\nThe generous 2.28 acre site, is clearly bounded accessed by a private stone driveway leading to an enclosed yard, providing ample off-street parking. Arranged around the yard, courtyard fashion, is over 155 square metres of fully functional outbuildings including; general purpose sheds, workshop, stables, byre, pens, lean too, fuel store treatment yard with crush. Ideal for those with or seeking to become livestock owners, especially horses. To the front of the house is a large lawn the remainder of the land is laid out in 2 fields.\n\n \n\nThis convenient holding has a gentle gradient, West facing aspect C. 80 metres direct frontage onto the public road. Situated in a private peaceful rural area directly adjoining SAC pNHA habitat lands.\n\n \n\n2.5km to Redhills Village 2km to Cloverhill. 6km to both the much sought after villages of Ballyhaise Butlersbridge. Only 12.5km/15 minutes drive to Cavan Town. Under 2 hours to both Belfast Dublin. GPS: 54.08367, -7.343564.\n\n \n\nViewing Highly Recommended By Appointment Only. \n\n"
      },
